== how the accuracy regression was found (before ae30e57 the bf16-scan median was 1.01, failing the test's 1.0 bound)
bisect over the commits, same test file, TF32 off, median / 95% of the ratio above:
898aaf1 (hybrid-qwen35)  0.84 / 1.13
ad137b4                  1.01 / 1.46     <- scan kernels
fc18fae                  1.01 / 1.45
96642d9                  1.01 / 1.44
deb8670                  1.01 / 1.49
1bf1c9d                  1.01 / 1.46
per-parameter gradient error, new build / hybrid-qwen35 (same inputs; median over parameters), real model, ids seed 1:
ad137b4-era build                                   1.19
+ state products seeded with I u (as hybrid-qwen35)  1.03-1.08 (seeds 0-3)
  + old k_intra_bwd                                  1.08   (not the cause)
  + old k_dz_acc                                     1.07   (not the cause)
  + old k_intra_fwd                                  1.003
  + only its decay cumsum in the old order           1.003 / 0.998 (seeds 1, 2)
final (ae30e57)                                      1.004 / 1.000 (seeds 1, 2)
with ARMT_GEMM_TUNE=0 in both builds the gap before the cumsum fix was the same (1.061 / 1.045): not the GEMM choices.
kbench (one layer, random data) showed none of this: error vs an fp32 kbench build equal to hybrid-qwen35's on every
tensor (median ratio 1.00), at batch 2 and 8, seeds 1-5; both builds deterministic up to atomics (<= 4e-7).

